      "message": "It is weird to call TetheringMannager#startTethering here.\n\nI think more clean way is implement this feature outside of EthernetTracker.\n\nThere are two options I can think of:\nOption 1, have a separate service (ExtendedEthernetService ?) to handle this feature:\n    1. When permanent ethernet tethering feature enabled,  ExtendedEtherentService call EthernetManager#requestTetheredInterface(executor, TetheredInterfaceCallback) to keep ethernet in server mode and call TetheringManager#startTethering to trigger ethetnet tethering.\n    2. If TetheredInterfaceCallback#onAvailable get called, call TetheringManager#startTethering to enable ethernet tethering again.\n    \nOption 2, have new API in TetheringManager to start/stop permanent ethernet tethering, then tethering won\u0027t release EthernetIfaceRequest till permanent ethernet tethering is stopped.",
